ng. The `ast` module combined with careful exception management can handle order of operations safely while maintaining readability. I'll implement a version that preserves the expected behavior from the example.\n\nThe key considerations are:\n- Using `eval()` in an educational context where input is trusted\n- Handling ZeroDivisionError properly\n- Ensuring parentheses work correctly (ast.parse handles this naturally)\n\nLet me create a clean, working solution that meets all requirements while remaining practical for real-world use cases where input validation exists.",
